Feature: Layouts
  A game of Towers is played on a layout. The layout says where the towers stand and which lanes
  join them. The valley has five towers. The chain has eleven: the five of the valley, and an
  [[outpost]] halfway along each of the three lanes, on each side of the field. A team holds its
  home tower at the start, and no team holds an outpost.

  An outpost is a small tower. A drone takes it in the same way as any other tower: it circles
  the tower until the control is at the end of the bar. An outpost gives one point each second.
  Its radio shadow is only 50 m round it, so a drone can fly past it and stay in contact.

  Expectation: The valley has five towers
    Given the layout is the valley
    Then the towers in the game are 5

  Expectation: The chain has eleven towers
    Overrides: The valley has five towers
    The six new towers are outposts, three on each side of the field.

    Given the layout is the chain
    Then the towers in the game are 11
    And the Blue west outpost is neutral

  Expectation: One drone takes an outpost in 20 seconds
    Overrides: The chain has eleven towers
    The outpost is neutral at the start, and Blue holds it after the drone has taken it.

    Given the layout is the chain
    And the Blue drones in the Blue west outpost circle are 1
    When the game runs for 20 seconds
    Then the Blue west outpost is held by Blue
